<title>CANADA: WCE governors ok transgenic canola deliveries.</title>
<headline>WCE governors ok transgenic canola deliveries.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transgenic canola was approved Wednesday for delivery against Winnipeg Commodity Exchange futures contracts by the board of governors, according to a statement issued by the exchange.</p>
<p>Transgenic canola deliveries will be accepted at the start of the 1997/98 (Aug/July) crop year.</p>
<p>&quot;This decision reflects the general acceptance of transgenic canola varieties by the marketplace. Currently, there are a number of varieties that are registered for production in Canada with numerous new varieties pending approval,&quot; WCE marketing director Bruce Love stated.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548))</p>
